{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794611147,"nonce":"Lsr50KW7ld2NCXbsoqe8BhrXgO0=","title":"CSS transitions are not carried by rows","message":"The keyframe case is carried (see the closed issue on CSS transform animations); transitions are not. A transition's node already holds its final transform and opacity in its props, so a binding would have to carry the difference from that final pose, not the absolute values: translate difference, scale ratio and turn difference about the node's centre, as the rows already compute from a binding and its baked values. Hover and focus transitions are the common source (cn buttons, cards), and the long ones are on nodes with text, which are painted in full on every frame today.\n\nNeeds: the difference taken against the node's resolved style at the moment the transition starts, a binding released when it ends with the final props written once, and the same checks as for keyframes (no own transform-origin, not inside an overlay root, no opacity). animation_paths.rs has transition_scene to hold it to the full paint.\n\nRelated: 122c606, efa5528.","files":null}]}